<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The moderate FID performance may be due to using low-pass filtered versions of the images to extract domain-invariant features during training. Low-pass filters may not fully eliminate domain-specific information, which leads to retention in the hidden representations produced by the contrastive model. We can use more sophisticated domain-invariant feature extractors <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> that could further improve performance. However, based on the results of the faithfulness metrics, we infer that the contrastive model is effectively guiding the diffusion process to preserve domain-invariant features, while also reducing training overhead.The improved per-iteration training time of Contrastive-SDE can be attributed to the use of domain-invariant features during training. Extracting domain-specific features by training a classifier is inherently more challenging than training on domain-invariant features with a contrastive loss, since the latter focuses on learning generalizable patterns that are less complex to model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Ablation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Choice of Initial time <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
Fig <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Ablation ‣ 5 Results &amp; Discussions ‣ Contrastive-SDE: Guiding Stochastic Differential Equations with Contrastive Learning for Unpaired Image-to-Image Translation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates an inverse relationship between <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and image faithfulness: as <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> increases, realism improves, but faithfulness declines.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.03821v1/abl.png" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:510/222;" width="510" height="222" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Comparison of faithfulness with initial time <math id="S5.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Choice of Score function <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.3 Ablation ‣ 5 Results &amp; Discussions ‣ Contrastive-SDE: Guiding Stochastic Differential Equations with Contrastive Learning for Unpaired Image-to-Image Translation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows the effect of score function on metrics on different <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
